  "vo": [
    {
      "id": "V1",
      "text": "Mrs. Lan doesn't read English, and her power's been out two days. She just left a voice note. Watch the clock.",
      "start": "0:10.2",
      "end": "0:19.9",
      "window": 9.65,
      "words": 21,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 8.4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 131,
      "measuredSeconds": 9.75
    },
    {
      "id": "V2",
      "text": "She heard it read back in Vietnamese and said yes. The group's own rules, not the AI, set the amount: a hundred and fifty dollars. Two organizers sign.",
      "start": "0:19.9",
      "end": "0:32.4",
      "window": 12.5,
      "words": 28,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 10.84,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 134,
      "measuredSeconds": 12.5
    },
    {
      "id": "V3",
      "text": "Paid, into her Venmo, with a message in Vietnamese. Twenty-two point five seconds to the SUCCESS webhook, on our PayPal stand-in. The approvals came on cue; real neighbors take longer.",
      "start": "0:35.4",
      "end": "0:51.2",
      "window": 15.8,
      "words": 30,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 12,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 114,
      "note": "Starts 0.6 s before the cut to her phone: \"Paid,\" over the three paid phones, the cut in the pause after it.",
      "measuredSeconds": 15.8
    },
    {
      "id": "V4",
      "text": "This is Neighborline: a hotline, not a dashboard. After the Eaton fire, one LA mutual-aid network took three hundred requests overnight, in Instagram comments. Most still run on a volunteer's personal Venmo.",
      "start": "0:51.7",
      "end": "1:07.1",
      "window": 15.4,
      "words": 32,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 12.39,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 125,
      "measuredSeconds": 15.6
    },
    {
      "id": "V5a",
      "text": "Rosa asks for groceries, in Spanish. Same rules, two approvals.",
      "start": "1:07.7",
      "end": "1:13.7",
      "window": 6,
      "words": 10,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 100,
      "measuredSeconds": 6.15
    },
    {
      "id": "V5b",
      "text": "Her email has no PayPal account yet: unclaimed. She gets claim help in Spanish.",
      "start": "1:18.1",
      "end": "1:24.9",
      "window": 6.8,
      "words": 14,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 5.6,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 124,
      "note": "Starts 1.5 s before UNCLAIMED lands, so the word \"unclaimed\" is spoken just after it is on screen.",
      "measuredSeconds": 6.9
    },
    {
      "id": "V5c",
      "text": "She claims it. Success. Most payout systems stop at unclaimed; this one follows through.",
      "start": "1:25.0",
      "end": "1:32.2",
      "window": 7.2,
      "words": 14,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 5.6,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 117,
      "note": "\"Success.\" is spoken ~0.7 s after SUCCEEDED is on screen.",
      "measuredSeconds": 7.35
    },
    {
      "id": "V6",
      "text": "Someone posing as the organizers, with a Venmo handle one letter off? Approve is disabled on every phone. No money moves.",
      "start": "1:32.5",
      "end": "1:42.0",
      "window": 9.5,
      "words": 21,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 8.4,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 133,
      "measuredSeconds": 9.65
    },
    {
      "id": "V7a",
      "text": "Under the hood: the agents that talk to neighbors have no PayPal tools. One separate approval service holds the Payouts credentials, and it pays only on a record signed with the passkeys of two different organizers.",
      "start": "1:42.3",
      "end": "1:57.1",
      "window": 14.8,
      "words": 36,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 13.94,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 146,
      "note": "Runs over /trust and into the rail push (Shot 10).",
      "measuredSeconds": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "V7b",
      "text": "AI output is schema-checked, repaired once, or the neighbor is asked again.",
      "start": "1:57.5",
      "end": "2:03.5",
      "window": 5.95,
      "words": 12,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 4.8,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 121,
      "measuredSeconds": 6.15
    },
    {
      "id": "V7c",
      "text": "The batch ID is derived from the signed approval, so a double tap can't pay twice. Webhooks are signature-verified, and every payout is reconciled against PayPal Transaction Search. The test count is from a real run.",
      "start": "2:03.8",
      "end": "2:19.1",
      "window": 15.25,
      "words": 36,
      "wpm": 155,
      "estSeconds": 13.94,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 142,
      "note": "Card 2 under \"can't pay twice\", card 3 under \"signature-verified\", card 4 under \"reconciled … real run\".",
      "measuredSeconds": 14.7
    },
    {
      "id": "V10",
      "text": "For agent builders: the same guard ships as an MCP server. An AI agent asking to pay is refused without two humans' signatures. With them, it pays.",
      "start": "2:19.4",
      "end": "2:31.5",
      "window": 12.05,
      "words": 27,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 10.8,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 134,
      "measuredSeconds": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "V8",
      "text": "Donors give with PayPal or Venmo. The public report never names a neighbor, and every number comes from the ledger.",
      "start": "2:31.8",
      "end": "2:40.9",
      "window": 9.05,
      "words": 20,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 8,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 133,
      "measuredSeconds": 9.05
    },
    {
      "id": "V9",
      "text": "Neighborline is open source. Try the hotline yourself; the link is below. Because the morning after a storm, help should sound like your own language.",
      "start": "2:41.5",
      "end": "2:52.9",
      "window": 11.4,
      "words": 25,
      "wpm": 150,
      "estSeconds": 10,
      "fits": true,
      "needWpm": 132,
      "measuredSeconds": 11.4
    }
  ],
